They haven't officially said whether it will
start that second week in October like Season

00:00:32.820 --> 00:00:35.190
4 did or if it will be a different week.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:37.730
But it is confirmed for October in general.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:41.839
So let's just start with the new footage and
then I'm going to do my top 10 pieces of New

00:00:41.839 --> 00:00:44.019
Information we got during the special.

00:00:44.019 --> 00:00:48.080
The footage wasn't an official trailer, it
was just a quick 20 seconds of Carol, Tyreese

00:00:48.080 --> 00:00:52.800
and baby Judith on their way to Terminus,
they were simultaneously following the railroad

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:55.709
tracks and trying to avoid the giant Walker
parade.

00:00:55.709 --> 00:01:00.459
Which kind of reminded me of the giant parade
Daryl and Michonne ran into when they first

00:01:00.459 --> 00:01:02.940
heard the Terminus signal in the charger.

00:01:02.940 --> 00:01:09.030
I can't confirm it was the same herd, but
it definitely feels like a mass walker migration

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:13.140
has been happening in the last 16 episodes,
so hopefully something in this new Terminus

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.970
plot will pay that off.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:19.470
Those walkers that they were hiding from in
the clip were definitely headed toward Terminus

00:01:19.470 --> 00:01:20.470
too.

00:01:20.470 --> 00:01:23.800
Yes they walk slowly, but I've seen a few
behind the scenes images of the set where

00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:28.020
they shoot the Terminus scenes and it looks
like something goes down.

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:32.820
So real quick careful for potential spoilers.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.640
Just skip forward in the video like 25 seconds.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.780
This isn't confirmed, but just in case.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:41.120
As you can see in these pics, there's some
kind of giant explosion at Terminus, I think

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:44.630
it has something to do with the Survivors
trying to escape and it also might have something

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:47.190
to do with the walker parade reaching Terminus.

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:52.820
The first full trailer, like the first long
trailer, will debut at Comic Con.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:57.570
I'm expecting it to drop Friday July 25th.

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:02.150
That's just the day I expect the Walking Dead
panel to be on.

00:02:02.150 --> 00:02:11.239
Since Saturday is Marvel and DC all day in
Hall H. I will of course be doing a mega video

00:02:11.239 --> 00:02:12.239
breakdown for that.

00:02:12.239 --> 00:02:15.170
So now let's talk about the top 10 things
we learned in the special.

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:18.379
Number 10 - Terminus isn't a trap, it's a
Test.

00:02:18.379 --> 00:02:21.689
They talked a lot about the conceit of the
unlocked gate.

00:02:21.689 --> 00:02:26.310
Like, why if you're living in this kind of
a world with such huge chompy threats walking

00:02:26.310 --> 00:02:29.810
around, would you leave your front gate unlocked
for anything and everyone to stroll right

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:30.810
through?

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:34.189
The answer is that it's a test, the people
at Terminus are probably using that gate to

00:02:34.189 --> 00:02:38.140
see how you react to the creepiness of the
flowers and the unlocked gate.

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:42.450
Scott Gimple pointed out that there were roof
snipers and the Terminus people clearly have

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:45.139
been doing whatever it is they're doing for
a long time.

00:02:45.139 --> 00:02:47.180
So they have the routine down cold.

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:52.201
I think the interesting question is what are
a few ways you could fail the test, clearly

00:02:52.201 --> 00:02:53.201
Rick failed.

00:02:53.201 --> 00:02:57.900
Guns were drawn and he saw everyone wearing
the survivor's gear.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:01.459
Number 9 - Not All the People At Terminus
Are Creepy Cannibals

00:03:01.459 --> 00:03:05.109
Gimple definitely danced around the Cannibal
question, he didn't say flat out yes or no.

00:03:05.109 --> 00:03:06.723
But he gave this weird Luke Skywalker Stormtrooper
analogy.

00:03:06.723 --> 00:03:08.640
There were a few funny Star Wars references
during the special.

00:03:08.640 --> 00:03:13.319
He said that had Luke be allowed to got the
academy in episode 4 like he wanted, he'd

00:03:13.319 --> 00:03:16.799
have become a Stormtrooper and worked on the
Death Star like any other person.

00:03:16.799 --> 00:03:23.379
That would have made him a bad person, it
would just have become his reality and he

00:03:23.379 --> 00:03:26.989
would have gone on making decisions using
the same logic he did back on Tatooine.

00:03:26.989 --> 00:03:31.159
What I think that means is that a lot of the
people living at Terminus aren't creepy cannibals,

00:03:31.159 --> 00:03:36.150
it's just that due to circumstances they find
themselves surviving on the only thing available.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:40.510
They don't believe in what they're doing in
a creepy philosophical way, they're just trying

00:03:40.510 --> 00:03:41.709
to survive.

00:03:41.709 --> 00:03:43.349
Bottom line, they're not evil, they're victims
of circumstance just like the survivors.

00:03:43.349 --> 00:03:45.059
And even though Grimple wouldn't confirm people
were being eaten.

00:03:45.059 --> 00:03:46.059
Look at these freaking bones on the ground.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:48.480
Come on' what else could they be.

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.069
Number 8 - The Premiere will be explosive.

00:03:51.069 --> 00:03:58.010
I know a lot of you guys were theorizing Morgan
would return and save them some how or Carol

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.879
and Tyreese would show up and do something.

00:03:59.879 --> 00:04:04.769
Both are possible, we did see the Walker Parade,
so that could be a factor.

00:04:04.769 --> 00:04:08.400
But I'm not expecting the survivors to escape
Terminus right away.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.739
I just think they'll get out of that train
car in those first two episodes.

00:04:11.739 --> 00:04:18.920
And yes, all the survivors in there are turning
into a pack of wild dogs, but I don't think

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:24.710
getting out of train car "A" is going to be
just a physical fight.

00:04:24.710 --> 00:04:28.360
I think they'll try to use Eugene's cure or
the lie that is the cure.

00:04:28.360 --> 00:04:32.760
He's a pretty fast talker and that mullet
is surprisingly disarming.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:37.000
Lauren Cohan and the producers just kept saying
that the early episodes would be crazy and

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:40.540
then there'd be a left turn, then crazy again,
then another left turn.

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:45.890
I just feel like they'll talk their way out
of the train, then discover all the cannibalism,

00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:49.120
then freak out again and carol and tyreese
will show up.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:54.240
Number 7 - People that we didn't think were
badass, get to be badass.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.860
Of all the people in the train car Lauren
Cohan could have been talking about, I think

00:04:57.860 --> 00:04:59.240
she was referring to was Tara.

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:03.110
No matter what I just don't equate Eugene
with potential badass.

00:05:03.110 --> 00:05:07.150
Tara on the other hand is one of those people
who's been like a deer caught in the headlights.

00:05:07.150 --> 00:05:10.281
She got injured on the way to Terminus and
she's been super depressed about the whole

00:05:10.281 --> 00:05:15.020
Governor thing so I'm really hoping to see
her get some hero moments in the premiere.

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:17.480
Aisha Tyler was talking about the Three Questions.

00:05:17.480 --> 00:05:21.210
It's all about weeding out the weak people,
the ones that don't have the potential to

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:24.650
survive or contribute to everyone's survival.

00:05:24.650 --> 00:05:28.140
Tara seems like someone who will get there,
she just hasn't been pushed over the edge

00:05:28.140 --> 00:05:29.190
far enough.

00:05:29.190 --> 00:05:35.730
I think the train car will be that push, I
want to see her go crazy on some Terminus

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:38.230
people.

00:05:38.230 --> 00:05:41.940
Number 6 - We will learn what happened to
Beth quickly

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.030
That is to say we won't have to wait long.

00:05:44.030 --> 00:05:48.320
I don't know if she's going to be in the first
episode, but it sounds like she they're saying

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:49.710
we'll know what's up really soon.

00:05:49.710 --> 00:05:53.990
Last year I saw a lot of rumors for her character
arc this season.

00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:56.640
They just said that she would be turning into
more of a leader.

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:01.241
Which fits with Lauren Cohan's comments that
people previously not seen to be badass, will

00:06:01.241 --> 00:06:02.870
be badass.

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:06.610
Beth was getting pretty mean with Daryl's
crossbow until she got snatched.

00:06:06.610 --> 00:06:10.060
Supposedly, she's going to show up somewhere
outside of Terminus.

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:14.260
It may or may not be with Seth Gilliam's new
character, the father Gabriel person we've

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:15.860
seen on the set.

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:18.910
Number 5 - The Funeral Parlor was not a trap

00:06:18.910 --> 00:06:22.920
I loved the explanation that it belonged to
this very nice funeral director who was just

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:27.660
cleaning up bodies and burying them until
one day he just got killed on one of his runs.

00:06:27.660 --> 00:06:31.340
They cut it out during the script phase, so
it was never filmed, but I think that means

00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:35.400
the dogs we heard and Beth's kidnapping were
unrelated.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:39.570
No one was using the house as a way to trap
people and take them to Terminus.

00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:41.122
The thing that really set off those rumors
was all the food there.

00:06:41.122 --> 00:06:42.130
And the fact it looked so organized.

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:45.920
Not at all what we saw in the other homes
people went in during the season.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:51.570
Number 4 - They'll be jumping around in the
comics, it's not all going to be a linear

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:52.570
adaptation.

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:56.210
Right now where we are in the show is right
around where the Hunters appear in the comics.

00:06:56.210 --> 00:06:59.680
But Gimple said that they were going to do
a scene from way way back in the comics too,

00:06:59.680 --> 00:07:04.110
so it's not like you can just go forward one
issue of the comic for each episode.

00:07:04.110 --> 00:07:05.730
That's not a huge surprise, since they change
stuff from the comics all the time.

00:07:05.730 --> 00:07:08.840
And even when they do straight up adaptations,
like Rick biting that guys neck.

00:07:08.840 --> 00:07:10.720
It's not exactly like it is in the comics.

00:07:10.720 --> 00:07:15.360
I am really curious what that scene is, the
one from way way back.

00:07:15.360 --> 00:07:19.400
It might be a flashback scene because they
did a lot of of those in season 4.

00:07:19.400 --> 00:07:24.670
I think my favorite was Michonne's when she
was thinking about her life when Andre was

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.020
still alive.

00:07:26.020 --> 00:07:28.350
Number 3 - Rick Will Let A Little of The Governor's
viciousness in

00:07:28.350 --> 00:07:32.400
They spent a lot of time talking about the
similarities between Rick and the Governor

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:35.460
and made it sound like if the Governor hadn't
lost his daughter.

00:07:35.460 --> 00:07:37.270
He'd have made a better leader than Rick.

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:40.810
Rick's biggest problem according to Gimple
is that he makes too many decisions based

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:42.350
on emotions.

00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:47.120
He doesn't have that creepy calmness that
Gareth is giving off.

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:51.791
And now that he's just bit someone's ear off
and killed the famer Rick inside him, he's

00:07:51.791 --> 00:07:54.130
probably going to get even crazier.

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:58.770
Not like looney tunes crazy, just much quicker
to take violent action.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:02.820
Number 2 - Terminus will be the biggest threat
the survivors have faced.

00:08:02.820 --> 00:08:06.540
I was surprised when they said that, because
the Governor and Woodbury were a pretty huge

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:10.030
threat and that tank assault last season was
a pretty big deal.

00:08:10.030 --> 00:08:15.130
The reason they gave for the comment was that
the Terminus people have a well oiled system

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:20.050
for processing people and threats it seems.

00:08:20.050 --> 00:08:25.090
I just wonder how they'll deal with that giant
walker parade that Carol and Tyreese are bringing.

00:08:25.090 --> 00:08:28.230
No amount of roof snipers will be able to
stop that.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:31.910
and my number 1 thing - Gareth is explained

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:35.450
Andrew West had that really cool interview
where he spelled Gareth out pretty clearly.

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:40.820
He's going to try and open the survivors up
to this new way of life and what life can

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:42.831
be in the world they're living in.

00:08:42.831 --> 00:08:46.270
That sounded really hippy new agey and weird.

00:08:46.270 --> 00:08:51.760
But what I think it means is that yes, he's
a cannibal and he's going to try and get everyone

00:08:51.760 --> 00:09:00.220
to go cannibal, just like a vegan would try
to convince you it's way healthier than not

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:01.330
eating animal protein.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:05.200
And he's going to try and get everyone hyped
about the weird co-op sustainable community

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:06.410
he's got going at Terminus.

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:09.720
It sounds a lot like he's a creepy cult leader
who's going to try to brainwash them into

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:10.720
cannibalism.

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:13.880
But let me know what your favorite moment
was during the special, and about that new

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:14.880
footage of Carol's group.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:17.840
What do you think they're going to do when
they get to Terminus?

00:09:17.840 --> 00:09:23.110
I'm betting on them unleashing walkers on
the fences, just like the walkers started

00:09:23.110 --> 00:09:27.520
taking down fences at the prison.

